1. Overview
This document goes over the steps needed to reproduce the results using the raw participants data.
Due to the experiment involving human subjects who completed tasks manually, all 
calculations were performed manually. No scripts or pipelines were required.

2. Data Preparation
2.1
The raw data file (data/raw_data.csv) contains several columns identifying the type of student the subject was
the rest recorded the programs answers and times.

2.2 Data Cleaning
The following steps were performed:
    I. Removed all rows that didn't involve the subjects answer or times they took
    II. Confirm that no participants data is missing
    III. Remove all participants whose answers don't reach an evaluated score of 7 or higher
    IV. Convert time values to numerical seconds
    V. Save cleaned data to data/cleaned_data.csv

3. Descriptive Statistics
3.1 Mean Completion Time:
    Program 1 mean: 49.6 seconds
    Program 2 mean: 60.1 seconds

4. Paired Sample t-Test:
4.1 Compute Difference Scores
    difference = program 1 time - program 2 time

4.2 Calculate Average Mean Differnce

4.3 Calcualte Standard Deviation of Difference

4.4 Calculate Standard Error:
    SE = Standard Deviation / sqrt(number of participants)

4.5 Compute the t-Statistic:
    t = Mean Difference / Standard Error

4.6 Find Degrees of Freedom:
    df = number of participants - 1

4.7 Calculate p-value:
    p = 2 X (1 - T(|t|, df))

5 Verification:
    Confirming that the means, t-value, and p-value match:
        - Program 1 mean: 49.6
        - Program 2 mean: 60.1
        - t(17) = -0.414
        - p = 0.68